# Courier Scan Package Page – UI Implementation Rule

## Objective

Build the Courier Scan Package Page (`/courier/scan`) for the Ashraf Courier Business Platform.  
**Purpose:** Provide a seamless, accessible interface for couriers to scan package barcodes/QR codes, view package details, update status, and capture GPS location.

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)
- **Naming & Scoping:** All IDs and classes must follow the [Naming & Scoping Rules](./naming-and-scoping.mdc) (`parcego-` prefix for IDs, `parcego-` BEM/SMACSS for classes).

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Core Features

- **Camera Viewfinder Overlay**
  - Live camera preview for barcode/QR scanning (mobile-first, fallback to file upload on desktop)
  - Overlay with scan area highlight
  - Accessible controls for starting/stopping scan
  - All elements must have unique IDs (e.g., `parcego-scan-viewfinder`, `parcego-scan-start-btn`)

- **Manual Tracking Number Input Fallback**
  - Input field for manual entry if scan fails
  - Accessible label, clear button, and submit button
  - Unique IDs (e.g., `parcego-scan-manual-input`, `parcego-scan-submit-btn`)

- **Package Details Display**
  - Show package info after successful scan/input (mock data)
  - Card layout with tracking number, recipient, address, status
  - Unique IDs (e.g., `parcego-scan-package-card`, `parcego-scan-package-status-badge`)

- **Status Update Buttons**
  - Prominent buttons for "Pickup", "In Transit", "Delivered"
  - Use shadcn/ui Button, with unique IDs (e.g., `parcego-scan-status-pickup-btn`)
  - Visual feedback for current status

- **GPS Location Capture**
  - Display current GPS coordinates/address (mocked)
  - Button to refresh location, with unique ID (e.g., `parcego-scan-gps-refresh-btn`)
  - Show error if location unavailable

---

## 3. Navigation

- Use Next.js App Router for navigation.
- All navigation and state changes handled client-side (no server calls).

---

## 4. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder.
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication.
- Use mock data for package details and status updates.

---

## 5. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.
- **IDs:** All HTML IDs must be globally unique and follow the format:  
  `parcego-[component]-[purpose]-[unique-identifier]`
- **Classes:** All classes must be BEM/SMACSS, prefixed:  
  `parcego-block__element--modifier`

---

## 6. Deliverables

- `/courier/scan` page and all required UI components.
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running the frontend demo.

---

## 7. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by project lead.

---

## 8. Example Naming

```jsx
<div id="parcego-scan-viewfinder" className="parcego-scan__viewfinder">
  <button id="parcego-scan-start-btn" className="parcego-scan__btn--start">Start Scan</button>
</div>
<input id="parcego-scan-manual-input" className="parcego-scan__input" />
```

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern Courier Scan Package UI, ready for future backend/API integration.

